{% comment %}
  OB: PDP size-guide entry point ("Maatadvies"), mirroring SweatyBetty's
  sb-size-chart trigger/dialog split (see ../SweatyBetty/snippets/sb-size-chart.liquid).

  The trigger must sit inside the size option's legend while the dialog must
  live outside the fieldset, so the caller renders this twice with `surface`
  and both computes the same derived id.

  Measurement tables are NOT built yet. Until a table exists for a size family
  the trigger is withheld entirely rather than opening an empty dialog — a
  trigger that opens nothing reads as broken, which is worse than no trigger.
  Fill `ob_size_chart_available` (and the table markup) when the real data
  arrives; placement and styling are already final.

  Accepts:
  - option: {Object} the size product_option (kind-detected by the caller)
  - surface: {String} 'trigger' | 'dialog'

  Usage (size options only, from product-variant-picker.liquid):
  {% render 'ob-size-chart', option: option, surface: 'trigger' %}
  {% render 'ob-size-chart', option: option, surface: 'dialog' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  capture ob_size_kind
    render 'ob-option-meta', option_name: option.name, field: 'size_kind'
  endcapture
  assign ob_size_kind = ob_size_kind | strip

  assign ob_dialog_id = 'ob-size-chart-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: option.position

  comment
    No size family has a measurement table yet. Flip a family to true here (and
    add its table below) as the data lands; the trigger appears for exactly the
    families that can answer it.
  endcomment
  assign ob_size_chart_available = false
-%}

{%- if ob_size_chart_available -%}
  {%- unless surface == 'dialog' -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="ob-size-chart__open"
      data-ob-size-chart-open="{{ ob_dialog_id }}"
    >
      {%- render 'ob-icon', icon: 'ruler' -%}
      {{ 'products.product.size_guide' | t }}
    </button>
  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- unless surface == 'trigger' -%}
    <dialog
      id="{{ ob_dialog_id }}"
      class="ob-size-chart"
      closedby="any"
      aria-labelledby="{{ ob_dialog_id }}-title"
    >
      <h2 id="{{ ob_dialog_id }}-title" class="ob-size-chart__title">
        {{ 'products.product.size_guide' | t }}
      </h2>
      {%- comment -%} Table markup lands here with the real data. {%- endcomment -%}
    </dialog>
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
